# What the content table builders write (scripts/mods/content-tables.json) is
# stored and checked out with LF on every machine, because every builder writes
# LF. Without this a checkout with core.autocrlf true (One, the Windows runners)
# held these files CRLF, so each rebuild there rewrote every one of them whether
# it changed or not, and a table that pins its inputs by sha256 pinned bytes no
# other checkout has (#3029). The catalogue's pages, which Build-NpcPopulation.py
# writes by hand with --write-runtime (writesOffChain), are written LF the same
# way (#3120). tests/test-3029-builder-eol.js holds this list to
# content-tables.json. What ships still goes out as scripts/release/ShippedBytes.ps1
# reads it, whatever the checkout.
game/data/** text eol=lf
game/gamemode.js text eol=lf
game/gamemode-tables/** text eol=lf
game/plugins/thornswood-front.js text eol=lf
docs/systems/** text eol=lf
tests/fixtures/merchant-retrieval-records.json text eol=lf
docs/HUNTING-SPOTS.csv text eol=lf
docs/NPC-SPAWNS.csv text eol=lf
docs/NPC-POPULATION.md text eol=lf
# Except the recipe for Thornswood-Last.esp (#2791), which is bytes and not
# text: a line end turned inside it would make a recipe that builds nothing.
game/data/last-plugin.recipe -text !eol

# The licence texts of the vcpkg libraries in the client files (#3099), byte
# for byte as vcpkg installed them: records\client-licences.json holds each
# by sha256, and the downloads carry them as they are, so no checkout may
# turn their line ends.
records/client-licences/** -text
# The same for the npm packages' texts in build.js (#3751), which
# records\front-build.json holds by sha256.
records/front-licences/** -text

# The pre-push hook (#5291) is read by sh, Git for Windows' too, which needs
# LF line ends; tests/test-5291-pre-push.ps1 holds it.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
